.env
*.log
.DS_Store

# Anywhere, not only under frontend/. A tool run from the root makes a second
# node_modules there, and a cache file out of it once reached a commit: the rule
# lived in frontend/.gitignore, which does not cover the root.
**/node_modules/

# Per-session working copies made by tooling, never part of the repo. The
# leading ** matters: a pattern with a slash inside it is anchored to the root of
# the repository, so .claude/worktrees/ never covered frontend/.claude/worktrees/,
# which is the directory the rule was written for.
**/.claude/worktrees/

# How a machine happens to start the dev server, which is a fact about one
# machine and not about the portal: the tooling writes it when a preview is
# opened, and a checked in copy would fight anybody whose ports differ.
**/.claude/launch.json
